# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20 side quest: The Powder Keg Ledger. Weston Murdoch's list of who the hysteria will take; the party crosses names off before the seventh dawn.

~ start
Narrator: Weston Murdoch stands at the church door with an open ledger in his hands, the warm light gone from his face.
weston_murdoch [sad]: This fever breaks on the seventh dawn, friends. One neighbour dead and one roof burned, and twice that every week after. I already know the first names.
* Who is on your list? -> names
* Let us help you cross those names off. -> accept
* We are already looking for the root of this madness. -> END

~ names
weston_murdoch [weary]: Jeremiah Stover, because the crowd swears he hides strangers in his cellar. And the old schoolhouse, for it has the driest roof in the village.
-> start

~ accept
approve tobin_hayward +3 rook_coldwake +2: You took Weston's ledger to save Jeremiah and the schoolhouse
set rk_ledger_asked
quest powder_keg_ledger asked
weston_murdoch [smile]: Take this book. Get Jeremiah out of sight, soak the schoolhouse shingles, and may the Brightsinger keep us all.
-> END

~ progress
if days_since.hysteria_began >= 7
if flag.rk_jeremiah_hidden or flag.rk_school_saved
quest powder_keg_ledger done
weston_murdoch [weary]: One line drawn through, at least. That is one soul or shelter spared that would have gone to the ash.
-> END
else
quest powder_keg_ledger burned
weston_murdoch [sad]: The seventh dawn came, and the page stayed clean of ink. I hold no blame in my heart for you, friends, though I cannot bear to meet your eyes.
-> END
endif
endif
Narrator: Weston turns the open ledger toward you, its paper smelling of damp wool and tallow. Two names wait on the page while the seventh dawn creeps closer.
-> menu

~ menu
* [if not flag.rk_school_saved] Organise a bucket line to wet the schoolhouse roof. -> school
* [if not flag.rk_jeremiah_hidden] Where is Jeremiah hiding right now? -> jeremiah
* [if flag.rk_jeremiah_hidden and flag.rk_school_saved] We have seen to both of them. -> both
* Leave the ledger for now. -> END

~ school
* [Athletics DC 12] Haul the water up to the schoolhouse roof ourselves. -> school_ok | school_poor
* [if gold >= 20] Pay Beatrice Wells twenty gold for her rain barrels. -> school_paid
~ school_poor
Narrator: Buckets clatter against the cobbles and cold water sloshes over your boots. The high slates above remain bone dry.
-> menu
~ school_paid
gold -20
-> school_ok
~ school_ok
set rk_school_saved
Narrator: Water streams down the black slates and rises in a thin, mossy steam against the night air. If a torch lands up there tonight, it will find nothing to bite.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good wet slate now. Not a stray spark takes root on my watch.
-> menu

~ jeremiah
weston_murdoch [neutral]: You will find Jeremiah crouched behind the hay carts in the Round. Tell the stubborn old man to slip up the hill to me after dark.
-> menu

~ both
quest powder_keg_ledger done
weston_murdoch [smile]: My hand shakes, forgive me, it is only relief. Two crossed out, and the dark is a little lighter tonight.
-> END
